#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:95
#: 052253ca67f74d7db0bb0e8545da0f37
msgid "``scripts/motor-diagram-data/AP_Motors_display.json`` amplifies and/or overrides the data in ``AP_Motors_test.json`` for selected frame types. ``AP_Motors_display.json`` can be edited to alter the appearance of diagrams. Each field overrides the corresponding field in ``AP_Motors_test.json`` or adds amplifying information for display in the diagram."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:97
#: e66fe72fd31a42998ac4db63011727a0
msgid "After editing ``AP_Motors_display.json``, re-generate diagrams using ``build_motor_diagrams.py`` as described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:99
#: 6c063846b4d94ec8a84f186192a92cb5
msgid "All fields except class and frame IDs are optional (if not specified, values from ``AP_Motors_test.json`` are used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:101
#: 4078d807f38445d29829510e0fca5ce5
msgid "``ClassName`` and ``TypeName`` override the title text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:103
#: 8835b758d83642a0b520a48b45f51a06
msgid "``Notes`` are displayed below the title text as part of the diagram (smaller font)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:105
#: c4abae3872b843498150145b5e587ccd
msgid "``WikiNotes`` add a wiki ```.. note::``` block below the diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:107
#: d09a0b01bd784c078c2033a98b0affc1
msgid "``Comments`` are information only and ignored when generating the diagrams"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:109
#: 44fd6c22cc284c2a8888292364bd66e0
msgid "``Skip`` if true, this frame is skipped by the generator script (useful for frames that have duplicate diagrams)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:111
#: 6f88fa5acaa84d729b4dc56962da8ad7
msgid "``motors`` includes motor matrix data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:113
#: 5c93a5e00c114618b9647c66b18eb570
msgid "``Number`` is the intended motor output channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:115
#: 7bef851832784d0da85880a0f2986ca8
msgid "``TestOrder`` is the order in which the motor is tested (letters ``A``, ``B``, ``C``, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:117
#: 8d92ab6b07d847bcb0a80678f2eb050e
msgid "``Rotation`` is the motor rotation direction (CCW or CW). A ``?`` indicates no yaw torque."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:119
#: aae5268b443749838e414c03bbafd903
msgid "``Roll`` is the \"roll factor\" of the motor and functions as an X coordinate for the diagram. Positive is below the origin, and negative is above. Generally, use values between -0.5 and 0.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:121
#: 6c272be2da7841ce80395c48d7b5a102
msgid "``Pitch`` is the \"pitch factor\" of the motor and functions as a Y coordinate for the diagram. Positive is to the right, and negative is to the left. Generally, use values between -0.5 and 0.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-generating-motor-diagrams.rst:123
#: da0924802f5c4b36be91132377e0f5da
msgid "``FrameLines`` can be used to override the default frame arm depiction, where each motor is connected to the center of the frame. The coordinate system functions the same as for ``Roll`` and ``Pitch``."
msgstr ""

